<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I'm having a similar issue with my DM1701 on the 20241215 fw build.   I can xmit to my MMDVM most of the time (it can get finicky), but when I go to Calibrate to check BER, Xmit fails.    <br><br>UPDATE:   This post might have the answer:  <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=19&amp;t=4626" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=19&amp;t=4626</a><br><br>I'm gonna try this tonight - check calibration of my radio against my SDR radio.     <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile">    K7KS</div></blockquote>Using the SDR is IMO the best option, unless you happen to have a high resolution counter.<br><br>Most counters only seem to resolve to 1kHz, which isn't good enough when calibrating multiple radios to work with the same hotspot, as the Hotspot Rx window is only around +/- 200Hz at most.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Jan 24, 2025 6:03 am</p><hr />
