		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Baofeng DM-1701; receives DMR; transmit DMR fails]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4765&amp;p=35148#p35148"><![CDATA[
My DM-1701 receives DMR talkgroups from a WPSD hotspot fine. Transmit to the hotspot (and up into the talkgroup) fails. The HT had the same problem on the OEM firmware, and I had hoped upgrading to OpenGD77 might fix it.<br>Today I am tinkering with the calibration settings on the radio screen. Likely my last attempt with the radio.<br>Over weeks I adjusted the hotspot - its BER and signal adjustments, frequency assignment, various antennas, etc. I am confident in my hotspot configs, which are validated by separate success on Alinco and Yaesu stock HTs.<br>The DM-1701 currently Rx/Tx no problem on FM repeaters and simplex. Monitoring a kerchunk to the hotspot on FM set to the simplex freq - I can hear a helicopter blade thumping sounding hiss. The DM-1701 is resulting in a Tx, but no intelligible signal to the hotspot.<br><br>Has anyone seen this problem before? And how to fix?<br><br>At this point, I am fine tossing the DM-1701 on the shelf of analog HTs. However, based on the community activity and documentation, I know people are getting these radios running.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7694">N0NV</a> — Wed Jan 15, 2025 12:47 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
